{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>His corpse shall not remain overnight on the tree.</b> Rather, <b>you shall surely bury him</b> on that very day he was hanged, lest the onlookers say that the case of one executed for blasphemy was by hanging, and perhaps this one too was a blasphemer, and it is a disgrace to the King. Another interpretation: <b>for a curse of Elohim is he who is hanged</b> — one may say, if he treated lightly the commandments of the Holy One, blessed be He, he has already taken his due through death, and it suffices that he was hanged. Another interpretation: it refers to the judges — if he remains on the tree and passersby see his face and stature, sometimes they may suppose he was sentenced for a light offense, and will curse the judges who sentenced him to hanging." "<b>For you shall surely bury him on that day.</b> And let no one become defiled through it by touching or overshadowing." "<b>Has given you as an inheritance.</b> This law applies only in the land of the seven nations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:44.435342128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}